{"availability":"available","full":"ralforion/orionbelt-semantic-layer","name":"orionbelt-semantic-layer","description":"Source-available semantic and context layer, rule engine, and semantic sidecar for agentic AI and governed analytics. Compiles declarative YAML models into optimized SQL, KPIs, and semantic context across 8 SQL dialects.","category":"Business","language":"Python","stars":99,"forks":10,"created":"2026-02-10T16:10:48Z","updated":"2026-10-05T20:43:47Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://ralforion.com/orionbelt-semantic-layer/","topics":["agentic-ai","analytics-as-code","bigquery","business-intelligence","clickhouse","data-analytics","databricks","dremio","duckdb","headless-bi","mcp","mcp-server","metrics-layer","mysql","postgresql","semantic-layer","semantic-sidecar","snowflake","text-to-sql","yaml"],"demo":"https://orionbelt.ralforion.com/ui/?__theme=dark","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:22.008Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:22.008Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:22.008Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:33:22.008Z","stars":99,"forks":10}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Define your metrics once in YAML. Let agents and BI tools query them without ever touching your schema.","A semantic sidecar: it rides alongside the systems you already run instead of replacing them.","Ask an LLM to write SQL against a raw star schema and sooner or later it joins two fact tables and hands you a revenue number inflated by a factor of eight. It looks right. Nobody catches it."],"features":["Business rules state conditions over the model's dimensions, measures and metrics: who counts as a high-value client, which categories must not sell at a loss. The rule engine compiles each rule to the query that…","External concept mappings link data objects, dimensions, measures, metrics and rules to the concepts your organisation already governs (schema.org, FIBO, an internal vocabulary), with provenance.","The OBSL graph exposes every loaded model as RDF, so its artefacts, joins, rules and concept links can be queried with SPARQL.","Lineage shows what a dimension, measure, metric, rule or query is built from, down to the tables and the joins the planner chose, as JSON, Mermaid, or Turtle linked into the OBSL graph, in the API, the CLI (obsl…","Descriptions, synonyms and owners on each artefact give agents the vocabulary users actually speak."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ralforion/orionbelt-semantic-layer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2ce5c27431f92b2c18cb44a5bb2c5815d5ef43dc2fa5d03676bc964946fb5396","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:22.267Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:22.267Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Define your metrics once in YAML. Let agents and BI tools query them without ever touching your schema.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ralforion/orionbelt-semantic-layer/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"You self-host, across more than one engine, and want one model to compile for all of them.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ralforion/orionbelt-semantic-layer/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"OrionBelt Semantic Layer is source-available under BUSL-1.1 until its Apache-2.0 conversion — the free distribution has full parity on the shipped v2.6 surface and is production-grade for self-hosted use.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ralforion/orionbelt-semantic-layer/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"2ce5c27431f92b2c18cb44a5bb2c5815d5ef43dc2fa5d03676bc964946fb5396","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ralforion/orionbelt-semantic-layer/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:22.268Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-05T20:43:47Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ralforion/orionbelt-semantic-layer/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-